
1.	Authentication
•	User registers or logs in.
•	A users/{uid} document is created with basic user info and role.
2.	Browse & Discovery
•	User enters MainLayout.
•	Main tabs:
•	Home
•	AI Chat
•	Cart
•	Profile
•	Home shows banners, categories, featured products, and search.
3.	Search & Product Discovery
•	User searches for a product or opens a category.
•	App fetches matching products from database.
•	User opens the product details page.
4.	Product Details
•	Page shows images, name, brand, price, stock, description, and fragrance notes.
•	User can add the product to cart.
•	Product events can be logged, such as product_view and add_to_cart.
5.	Cart
•	User reviews cart items.
•	User can increase, decrease, or remove products.
•	App checks stock before increasing quantity.
6.	Address & Checkout
•	User selects address from saved addresses or map picker.
•	In checkout, user reviews address, payment method, notes, and order summary.
•	User taps Place Order.
7.	Order Processing
•	App creates an order with pending status.
•	Backend stock-processing function verifies stock, deducts quantity, and updates order status.
•	Cart is cleared after success.
•	User tracks order in My Orders.
8.	Profile
•	Profile shows user info, order history, saved addresses, and logout.
•	includes edit profile and preference management.
9.	AI Chat Feature
•	User enters AI Chat and starts a new session.
•	Before giving recommendations, AI asks a few short qualifying questions to understand user taste and need.

•	User Sends a message, such as:
 o   “عايز عطر صيفي مناسب للافراح قوي ويكون ريحته فيه لمسة لمون ”
 o " I want a strong winter oud perfume suitable for university" 

• The AI responds based on the product catalog and injected business logic prompts.
•	AI then responds using product catalog data and business logic.
•	Chat sessions and messages are stored in database.
10.	AI Feedback Feature
•	After the conversation, a feedback sheet appears.
•	User submits:
•	Rating from 1 to 5
•	Was this helpful?
•	Optional comment
•	Feedback is stored under the same chat session.
11.	AI Feedback Analysis
•	A Cloudflare Worker reads the chat transcript, rating, helpfulness flag, and comment.
•	Worker sends them securely to an LLM.
•	LLM returns structured analysis:
•	intentUnderstood
•	needSatisfied
•	satisfactionScore
•	sentiment
•	failureReason
•	improvementSuggestion
•	missingNeeds
•	Analysis is stored in database.
12.	Admin Dashboard
•	Admin manages products, orders, banners, and general statistics.
•	Admin also views AI analytics such as satisfaction score, negative sessions, failure reasons, and difficult user queries.

